From: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] qwen3.8: sm80 thin-M BF16 GEMM for measured unquantized
 shapes

VLLM_QWEN38_THIN_GEMM (default 0 = unchanged). The GLM 5.3 split-K Triton
thin-M GEMM (FP32 accumulate, deterministic last-CTA reduction, pre-capture
warmup, capture fallback) for the projections the NVFP4 checkpoint leaves in
BF16, dispatched only for the (N, K, row bucket 1/4/8/16/32) cells where it was
measured >= 5 % faster than cuBLAS on CMP 170HX (GDN in_proj/ba, QSA qkvg/o,
indexer, HC down/up, shared expert, router). Every other shape and every batch
above 32 rows keeps F.linear. Not bitwise equal to cuBLAS (summation order);
max error against an FP64 reference is no larger than cuBLAS's.
---
